#!/usr/bin/env Rscript

# =========================================================================
# GSE72810 effect sizes and confidence intervals
# =========================================================================
#
# Purpose
#
# Calculate effect sizes and 95% confidence intervals for the four locked
# GSE72810 analyses generated by Script 47:
#
# 1. Primary fixed-module projection:
#    representative probes, all-146-sample z-reference,
#    23 definite bacterial versus 28 definite viral samples.
#
# 2. Primary-only z-reference sensitivity:
#    the same frozen representative probes,
#    51 definite bacterial and viral samples as the z-reference.
#
# 3. Expanded phenotype sensitivity:
#    40 definite-plus-probable bacterial versus
#    35 definite-plus-probable viral samples.
#
# 4. All-authorized-probe mean sensitivity:
#    all-146-sample z-reference,
#    23 definite bacterial versus 28 definite viral samples.
#
# For every analysis and locked module, this script calculates:
#
# - bacterial and viral group summaries;
# - median bacterial-minus-viral score difference;
# - Hodges-Lehmann location-shift estimate;
# - stratified nonparametric percentile-bootstrap 95% CI for the
#   Hodges-Lehmann estimate;
# - rank-biserial effect size;
# - stratified nonparametric percentile-bootstrap 95% CI for the
#   rank-biserial effect size;
# - Wilcoxon rank-sum P value;
# - within-analysis Benjamini-Hochberg FDR.
#
# Bootstrap resampling is performed independently within bacterial and
# viral groups. The locked modules, sample definitions, probe choices,
# scoring rules and expected directions are not changed.
# =========================================================================


